    - Tsongkhapa Thangka
    - "Siddh\u0101rtha Guatama"
    groupInfo:
    - "Group: Jainism\r\n\nContinent: Indian subcontinent\r\n\nArtist: Unknown\r\n\nYear:
      1850 AD\r\n\nMedium: Unknown\r\n\nSource: Jain Miniature\n    Painting\r\nLocation:
      Japiur, Rajasthan, \n    India\r"
    - "Group: Tibetan Buddhism \r\n\nContinent: Indian subcontinent\r\n\nArtist:
      Unknown\r\n\nYear: 18th Century\r\n\nMedium: Pigments on cloth\r\n\nSource:
      Kyi Monastery\r\n\nLocation: Tibet\r"
    - "Group: Buddhism\r\n\nContinent: Indian subcontinent\r\n\nArtist: Unknown\r\n\nYear:
      Unknown\r\n\nMedium: Unknown\r\n\nSource: P\u0101li Canon\r\n\nLocation: Unknown\r"
    groupShortInfo:
    - "\rBuddhism, followed by Buddhists, teaches the path to enlightenment through
      meditation and ethical living, based on the teachings of Siddhartha Gautama
      (Buddha). Jainism, practiced by Jains, emphasizes non-violence, truth, and
      asceticism, guided by the teachings of Mahavira."
    - Buddhism, followed by Buddhists, teaches the path to enlightenment through
