      of the\n    Kongo"
    - "Group: Mali Culture\r\n\nContinent: Africa\r\n\nArtist: woven by Mali men,
      \n    dyed by Mali women \nYear: 12th century   \r\n\nMedium: Mud painted cloth\r\n\nLocation:
      San, Mali\r"
    groupShortInfo:
    - Africa, the world's second-largest continent, is a cradle of human civilization
      and biodiversity. It features diverse cultures, languages, and landscapes,
      ranging from the Sahara Desert to the lush rainforests. Africa's rich history,
      music, art, and wildlife make it a continent of immense cultural and ecological
      significance.
    - Africa, the world's second-largest continent, is a cradle of human civilization
